  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x)=\\log _{5} \\log _{3} x,$ then $f^{\\prime}(e)$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jba62",
      "text": "$e \\log _{e} 5$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "aYqAL",
      "text": "$e \\log _{4} 3$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oUn6I",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{e \\log _{e} 5}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gZ3We",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{e \\log _{e} 3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have,\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} f(x) &=\\log _{5} \\log _{3} x \\\\ &=\\frac{\\log \\log _{3} x}{\\log 5} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\log \\left(\\frac{\\log x}{\\log 3}\\right)}{\\log 5} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\log \\log x-\\log \\log 3}{\\log 5} \\\\ f^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{1}{\\log 5} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\log x} \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(e) &=\\frac{1}{e \\log 5 \\cdot \\log e} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{e \\log 5} \\quad[\\because \\log e=1] \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{e \\log _{n} 5} \\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
